+
+## Voyage 3 — Re-entrant render guard
+
+**Defect:** External browser acceptance suite reports `NotFoundError: Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node'` when deleting a todo via empty edit. The `focusout` handler calls `saveEdit(li)` after the `keydown` handler has already removed the `<li>` from the DOM via `removeTodo` → `render()`. The `saveEdit` detached-node guard (`document.body.contains(li)`) is insufficient: in a real browser the `focusout` fires synchronously during the first `render()`'s stale-removal `removeChild`, when the `<li>` still appears attached. The second `render()` call (from `saveEdit` → `removeTodo` → `render`) removes the `<li>` first, and the first `render()`'s stale-removal snapshot then tries `removeChild` on an already-removed node.
+
+**Root cause:** `render()` in `js/app.js` has no `todoList.contains(node)` guard before `removeChild` in its stale-removal loop (line ~114). The `querySelectorAll` snapshot is stale by the time the loop reaches the node, because a re-entrant `render()` call already removed it.
+
+**Specs written:** `features/editing-conformance.feature` — new `@conformance` scenario `render checks containment before removing a stale list item`.
+
+**Watchbill:** `watchbill.json` targeting the new conformance scenario.
+
+**Next:** QM dispatch to implement the undefined step definition for the new conformance check and verify it goes red on current code, then Crew to add the `contains` guard in `render()`.
